id: ops-3wrp
title: Parallel jobs must not replace the shared global npm
description: "Deep and release workflows install the pinned npm globally after setup-node. On the shared local runners every container on a host shares the toolcache Node installation, so parallel jobs replace the same npm and fail with ENOTEMPTY or npm: command not found. GitHub issue unbraind/pm-ops#284."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ops#284","gh:unbraind/pm-ops#289"
created_at: "2026-11-16T14:40:51.350Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T08:29:13.703Z"
author: pi-glm
acceptance_criteria: "Every workflow installs the pinned npm with --prefix into a job-local directory and prepends its bin to the job path, keeping the exact-version assertion; A workflow-contract test fails if any workflow replaces the global npm; A regression test runs two overlapping pinned installs into separate prefixes against one shared Node directory and proves both stay at the pin with the shared npm untouched"
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T15:16:48.720Z",codex-sol,"Continuation: preserving the existing uncommitted implementation. Reviewing all bootstrap paths including Windows, strengthening the overlap proof, and rerunning all required gates to completion before the first push."
  "2026-11-16T15:27:14.297Z",codex-sol,"Root cause confirmed in the workflow source: global installation of the pinned npm replaces the same Node installation used by parallel jobs on a shared toolcache. Replaced each bootstrap with a job-local prefix, published only its bin directory to the job PATH, and retained exact-pin checks including a separate subsequent-step assertion. Workflow contracts reject global npm replacement across all workflow files. No runner settings or shared tool installations were modified."
  "2026-11-16T15:29:09.237Z",codex-sol,"Additional regression evidence: install processes must have overlapping lifetimes; both cold and warm rounds share a private package cache; each prefix reports the exact pin and reaches a clean npm ci. The unchanged-shared-installation check hashes every file in the shared npm package as well as checking the CLI timestamp and version. Windows uses the same prefix form with Git Bash path conversion; global npm replacement is no longer an allowed bootstrap exception."
  "2026-11-16T15:42:10.687Z",codex-sol,The first combined gate command hit its 20-minute timeout during shared-host disk contention and is not pass evidence. Retrying all gates to completion using memory-backed temporary fixtures and the existing harness deadline scale. Assertions and test selection are unchanged.
  "2026-11-16T16:07:41.065Z",codex-sol,"Typecheck and lint passed. The 52 workflow contracts, workflow-wide global-install guard and changelog:check passed together. The overlapping cold/warm install regression passed with full shared-package hash checks; its latest caller-configuration isolation run is active. Initial broad quick tests timed out under disk contention; replacement broad gates remain pending."
  "2026-11-16T16:11:57.169Z",codex-sol,"Implementation commit 3056e53d1488cef1be5854efe3956f0db417ebb1 contains the requested fix and package-owned regression contracts. Focused contracts and changelog verification passed; typecheck and lint or the existing docstring static gate passed. The first broad quick attempt timed out, and its replacement remains active. The shared runner dispatch hold is respected before publication. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-16T16:44:03.708Z",codex-sol,"The broad suite completed with 1672 passing tests and three failures. One failure is introduced by the new regression: its raw spawnSync import violates the existing bounded-capture inventory. Correcting it to use the package adapter and bounding streamed stderr. The input-reader subprocess timeout and missing policy fixture are separate validation gaps and will be rechecked without weakening their assertions."
  "2026-11-16T16:46:04.316Z",codex-sol,"Corrected the new regression to use the existing bounded spawnSync adapter and cap streamed stderr. Typecheck, lint and test compilation passed; all 11 subprocess and npm-isolation tests passed. The two other broad-suite failure classes passed all 28 isolated rechecks without source changes. The earlier broad run remains a failed run (1672 passed, 3 failed, 2 skipped), with a fresh full npm test run scheduled after this commit."
  "2026-11-16T17:01:02.889Z",codex-sol,"The final npm test rerun completed: 1677 tests, 1674 passed, 1 failed and 2 skipped. The new npm-isolation regression and bounded-capture inventory pass. The sole remaining failure is the existing lifecycle-policy non-vacuity fixture missing its synthetic policies.json; isolated rechecks passed all 28 tests. Follow-up ops-policy-fixture-missing tracks this separate full-suite failure. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/289 remains draft pending full validation; no broad green result is claimed."
  "2026-11-16T19:23:50.350Z",codex-sol,"Review round P: replace the workflow-wide regex with a dependency-free shell command parser and regression fixtures. Parse run scripts with existing yaml where available; preserve allowed prefix-local installs. Verify typecheck, lint or docstring, focused guard/workflow contracts and changelog checks before pushing. No review-thread actions."
  "2026-11-16T19:28:57.876Z",codex-sol,"Review round P addresses parser threads PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64FaID and PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64F1se with a test-only shell command parser and existing-yaml run extraction. Added 38 fixtures. Thread PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64F1si is addressed by child ready markers, a bounded two-worker barrier, and child-written install start/end timestamps; cold and warm intervals must overlap, and the full shared-npm package hash assertion is retained. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run lint PASS. Linked guard/workflow/real-overlap command passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress: 109 pass, 0 fail/cancel/skip/todo. changelog:check initially reported a stale top heading: the existing v2026.11.15 tag has a 2026-11-16 creator date. Canonical changelog:full refreshed only that generated date; changelog:check now PASS. Full-suite certification remains with CI. Review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-16T21:51:39.303Z",codex-sol,"Review round X: verified open PR 289 at c6843a6 after fast-forward pull. Checking helper capture against subprocess inventory and wrapper before edits; will preserve overlap synchronization and run focused tests and package gates."
  "2026-11-16T21:52:47.811Z",codex-sol,"Validated PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64GMES: the unmodified subprocess inventory fails with raw process capture: test/npm-prefix-child.ts. Switched only the helper import to ../subprocess.ts; the ready barrier and child-recorded overlap intervals remain intact."
  "2026-11-16T21:54:14.298Z",codex-sol,"Review round X validation passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress (exit 0): node --test test/subprocess.test.ts test/job-local-npm.test.ts; npm run typecheck; npm run build:test; npm run lint; npm run changelog:check. Both cold/warm synchronized overlapping install rounds succeeded and retained the shared npm hash, timestamp and version. The original inventory failure was reproduced before the one-line import fix. No thread response or resolution was made; exact-head remote CI remains unverified."
  "2026-11-17T01:51:18.188Z",codex-sol,"Review round AA: pulled and verified the open PR head. Source inspection confirms the reported guard gaps. Replace shell tokenization with conservative logical-line matching and step-only script extraction, with intended false positives and regression fixtures. Also verify shared launcher identity after each install round and restrict the GITHUB_PATH exception to the single approved write."
  "2026-11-17T02:02:12.616Z",codex-sol,"All three scoped threads verified valid: PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64L9am, PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64L9au, PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64L9ay. Replaced shell tokenization with conservative logical-line matching and step-only YAML extraction. Shared launcher existence/link target and package version/mtime/digest are checked after each cold and warm install round; removal/retargeting fixtures prove the launcher check is independent of package bytes. The publication interval exempts only one exact approved GITHUB_PATH write; extra-write and duplicate-bootstrap fixtures fail. Kept the later runtime check and bounded subprocess wrapper. Guard/release/job-local/subprocess suite: 83 passed before the final extraction fixture; final guard: 53 passed and real-workflow rescan: 1 passed. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, duplication and changelog:check passed. No dependencies added; no findings refused. Full-suite certification remains with CI."
  "2026-11-17T03:39:08.872Z",pi-claude,"Round AF follow-up on the fail-closed guard, from the pm-ado review threads PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864PGRG and PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864P73_ and the identical pm-lint threads PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn2, PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn6 and PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn7; this repository carries the same guard with the direct YAML dependency. All three findings were reproduced against the guard source first: a prefix bootstrap followed by '&& npm install -g npm@11.19.0', 'npm install -gpld npm@11.19.0' and step env NPM_CONFIG_GLOBAL=true were all accepted by the previous code.\n\n1. Segment-scoped prefix exception: run scripts now split into command segments at unquoted ;, &, | and newlines. The scanner tracks quote state across lines and $( … ) substitutions (which nest a fresh quoting context even inside double quotes), skips comments and here-document bodies (the workflow-scoped test in this repository uses here-documents, which are now skipped as non-delimiting text), and any script that cannot be delimited (unbalanced quote or substitution) fails closed as 'undelimitable command line'. The job-local prefix exception only covers the segment carrying it; rejected fixtures add 'npm install --prefix \"$RUNNER_TEMP/npm-11.19.0\" npm@11.19.0 && npm install -g npm@11.19.0' and 'npm install --prefix \"$RUNNER_TEMP/npm-local\" npm@11.19.0; npm install -g npm@11.19.0'. Approved bootstrap fixtures stay accepted.\n2. Combined short flags: any single-dash letter cluster containing g now marks global (rejected: 'npm install -gpld npm@11.19.0', 'npm install -dg npm@11.19.0'); 'npm install -D pnpm' and 'npm install -gpld pnpm' stay accepted.\n3. Workflow, job and step env compose for each step run, the step scope taking precedence; npm reads npm_config_* keys case-insensitively. npm_config_global set to anything other than false/0/empty, npm_config_location=global, a ${{ … }} expression value, or an unreadable env scope or entry forces every npm install in that run global unless its own segment carries a job-local prefix. Fixtures cover step env flow mapping, job env flow and block styles, workflow env, expression values, location=global, step-override (job \"true\" + step \"false\" accepted) and accepted \"false\"/\"0\"/\"\" values.\n\nGates: guard suite 62 passed; the workflow-scoped job-local-npm test ('no workflow replaces the shared global npm installation') passed, its subprocess-based pinned-install integration test is unchanged and left to CI; typecheck, test build, lint, duplication and changelog:check passed. Every workflow in the repository still scans clean; the ../subprocess.ts wrapper in the job-local tests is untouched. Full-suite certification remains with CI."
  "2026-11-17T05:22:28.806Z",codex-sol,"Round AH: implement conservative run-wide global configuration and markers, install-family aliases, redirect-safe prefix segmentation, and comment-free effective prefix exemptions. Preserve all existing rejected fixtures and approved bootstrap workflows; verify required package gates before releasing the claim. No review-thread mutations."
  "2026-11-17T05:30:27.259Z",codex-sol,"Round AH verification: 133 tests passed with zero failures, cancellations or skips (102 guard fixtures, release-workflow contracts, real cold/warm job-local npm overlap regression, and subprocess adapter tests). npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run lint, npm run duplication, npm run changelog:check and git diff --check passed. Threads PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64Qoco, PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64Q1tC, PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64Q1tH, PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64Q1tK and PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64Q1tQ are addressed. Run-wide configuration and markers, installing aliases, redirect preservation and comment-free effective prefix exemptions match the companion copies. All earlier rejected fixtures and approved bootstrap workflows are retained. The subprocess.ts wrapper remains in use. Protected item dates are unchanged. Exact-head CI remains pending; no review-thread actions, publishing or merges."
  "2026-11-17T07:47:37.131Z",pi-guard-1117aj,"Round AJ: replaced the guard's per-segment shell parser with a line-based fail-closed rule, identical to the other fleet repositories: logical lines only (continuations joined, newline-only splits), comment and here-document text scanned like any other text, install family extended with update/up/upgrade/udpate, markers covering single-dash g clusters, global-containing tokens, -L with any value and two-plus-letter prefixes of global/location, npm config set/set as a run-wide global signal (narrowed to a set token: a read-only 'npm config get globalconfig' line tripped the broader form), operands naming npm by substring or computed form (tarball URLs, x@npm:npm), exemptions restricted to exact approved bootstrap lines, and step-level rejection of GITHUB_ENV npm_config_* writes and global/location npmrc writes. The hand-rolled workflow extractor now consumes inert job-level sequence values such as needs lists, which the repository's daily release workflow uses; every workflow still scans clean. No test code spawns processes, so the subprocess wrapper was not needed."
  "2026-11-17T08:23:27.833Z",codex-sol,"Round AM verified against unchanged guard: punctuation and comment-continuation bypasses, operandless global installs, persistent npm config setters, and spaced YAML env keys reproduce. Quoted command words already reject; add explicit regression coverage. Keep line-based checks and exact raw-line bootstrap matching. Unresolved review threads: PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64L9am, PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64Utmi. Delegated npx finding is already rejected by Round AJ; preserve its rejected fixture. Run targeted gates directly; never execute linked PM tests. Preserve the existing test-session isolation import in the pm-vcs fixture."
  "2026-11-17T08:29:12.142Z",codex-sol,"Round AM targeted verification: 206 tests passed with zero failures, cancellations or skips. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/daily-release-workflow.test.ts => PASS; npm run typecheck => PASS; npm run lint => PASS; npm run changelog:check => PASS. Scripts absent: duplicates. All real workflows pass the guard; no bootstrap trailing comment was found. Guard source md5 d7ec9edd85b0c9fbe3d5a9f0e4d8d9e2 is identical across five packages. Fixture bodies match, retaining the required pm-vcs session-isolation import. Protected root item dates are unchanged; rejected fixtures are preserved. Same-class config persistence and spaced YAML env-key fixes from PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGg, PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64U3xi and PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGj were applied to every copy. Dedicated real-workflow audit: node --test test/job-local-npm.test.ts => PASS. PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M64L9am is already addressed by 7f77286: delegated npx is in rejected and returns a finding; retained unchanged. Full-suite certification remains with CI. Releasing this claim without closing the item."
